Description: GNOME companion for Samsung Galaxy devices on mainline Linux
 Galaxy Companion is the native GNOME settings application for Samsung Galaxy
 phones and tablets running a mainline kernel: S Pen status, remote modes and
 air actions, keyboard cover special keys, haptics, fingerprint enrollment,
 dual boot and system updates. It updates itself from its own releases,
 independently of the device's port. Each page appears only when the device has the
 hardware behind it. It replaces Tab Companion from the Galaxy Tab S9 Ultra
 port and keeps its settings.
